# One line per check that runs against the fixture. The self-test requires every
# one of these substrings to appear in the fixture's output, so a check that
# stops examining anything goes missing here and is named rather than passing
# silently. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This exists because an exit code proved only that *some* check fired: four
# checks were deleted outright and the runner's output was identical.
#
# Each line is matched with grep -F, so it is a literal substring and not a
# pattern. Keep them short and distinctive — long enough to name one check,
# short enough to survive a reworded message.

# covers: a live document declaring covers and naming nothing
covers is empty, so nothing watches it

# decision link symmetry: supersedes with no superseded-by coming back
has no superseded-by link back

# accepted on a proposed footing: an amendment in force against an unagreed rule
which it amends — is 'proposed'

# decisions cite symbols: a file:line citation that decays silently
cites a line number, not a symbol

# git zhi docs check: a link to a file that is not there
git zhi docs check

# implementing an accepted one: a commit trailer naming a proposed decision.
# The self-test writes that trailer when it git inits its copy.
the refinement gate was skipped

# declared floor vs installed binary: a manifest demanding a version that will
# never exist. This check was added to close the "nothing examined" class and
# was itself unreachable from the fixture until it learned to read $ROOT.
below the declared floor

# NOT COVERED, and this is the honest limit of this file.
#
# The product check runs `sh t/git-zhi-subcommands.sh`, which reads this
# repository's own skills/ rather than $ROOT's, so pointing it at the fixture
# would not test the fixture. It stays gated behind SELFTEST and is the one
# check that can still be deleted without the self-test noticing. Its absence
# is at least loud — a missing t/git-zhi-subcommands.sh is reported rather than
# skipped — but a neutered one is not.
